You cannot sneak yard waste onto your neighbor's property without their permission. It is best to check with your local waste management company to see if they offer any special services for disposing of yard waste, or look into composting as an alternative. Alternatively, you could offer to take the yard waste to the local dump yourself, but make sure to check the regulations and fees first.

If you are looking for ways to reduce the amount of yard waste in your yard, consider planting native plants that require less maintenance or starting a compost pile to break down organic materials naturally. Additionally, you can find creative uses for some types of yard waste such as using grass clippings as mulch or turning fallen leaves into leaf mold which can be used in gardens or potting soil.

